WEBVTT

00:06.150 --> 00:08.980
Whatever it is you want to see, 
I want to help you see it.

00:09.990 --> 00:12.960
If there's something you 
don't know, I'll teach you.

00:12.960 --> 00:17.130
Though, when you want to achieve something 
solely through your own efforts, I won't interfere.

00:18.570 --> 00:20.980
What kind of scholar will you become?

00:20.980 --> 00:23.790
I'm very much looking forward to finding out.

00:24.480 --> 00:27.420
Why do you take such good care of me?

00:30.840 --> 00:35.710
Perhaps because this may be the only 
good thing I am able to do in my life.

00:45.890 --> 00:47.040
Professor!

00:47.730 --> 00:49.310
Hey there, Rishe.

00:53.160 --> 00:54.520
Please stand back!

00:55.160 --> 00:57.190
This suspicious person has declared

00:57.190 --> 00:59.910
he will cause an act of violence 
in town at six this evening!

00:59.910 --> 01:01.740
It's just as he says.

01:02.170 --> 01:06.580
And you think that by doing so, Prince 
Arnold will hear of the power of black powder?

01:08.640 --> 01:09.840
That's right.

01:09.840 --> 01:13.280
Such an action will affect people 
unrelated to this matter!

01:13.280 --> 01:15.310
Yes, I understand that.

01:15.310 --> 01:16.220
Professor!

01:16.970 --> 01:19.970
Well, its unveiling demands as much.

01:20.940 --> 01:23.170
As it's something I have created...

01:23.690 --> 01:26.480
I must take responsibility for it.

01:27.330 --> 01:31.860
Even if it means causing 
misfortune for someone else.

01:34.510 --> 01:37.910
My own existence is just the same.

01:38.360 --> 01:40.320
I'm sorry, Rishe.

01:59.140 --> 02:03.610
The words of a person like me... shouldn't 
be taken at face value.

02:05.470 --> 02:09.810
Taking you on as my student was 
no more than a whim of mine.

02:14.230 --> 02:15.250
Sister!

02:22.130 --> 02:26.080
<i>I once asked the professor...</i>

02:26.470 --> 02:31.290
Is it truly impossible for a poison 
to bring someone happiness?

02:33.460 --> 02:36.550
<i>But instead of asking...</i>

02:37.870 --> 02:42.300
Professor, I may only have been 
your student for a brief time,

02:43.360 --> 02:46.680
but I can say this with certainty...

02:47.980 --> 02:52.120
even a poison can bring happiness to someone.

02:55.600 --> 02:59.740
My alchemy teacher once told me,

03:00.280 --> 03:05.160
"If one fails to take all variables into 
account, the experiment will fail."

03:06.830 --> 03:10.410
No matter how great an 
alchemist you may be,

03:10.410 --> 03:13.660
your results will not always 
be as you anticipated.

03:15.180 --> 03:16.210
That is because...

03:16.210 --> 03:21.090
it was impossible for you to 
comprehend the variable that I am.

03:21.760 --> 03:22.940
What are you saying?

03:35.020 --> 03:35.930
What is that?

03:38.190 --> 03:41.990
Professor, the things you 
create aren't only poisons.

03:42.420 --> 03:47.090
Even if you can only think of them as 
things which bring misfortune to others,

03:47.090 --> 03:50.870
if their method of use is changed, 
many other types of value appear.

04:10.640 --> 04:12.560
Colored flames?

04:14.000 --> 04:16.180
The black powder exploded in the sky?

04:17.300 --> 04:18.740
What is all this?

04:20.210 --> 04:25.660
I once looked for a simple way to 
differentiate between types of metals.

04:26.360 --> 04:31.950
At that time, someone showed me the 
beautiful aurora, and I remembered...

04:32.480 --> 04:36.680
When fire is applied to metal, 
it gives off a beautiful light.

04:38.400 --> 04:39.820
That's true.

04:39.820 --> 04:43.770
When metals are burned, the 
flames turn different colors.

04:43.770 --> 04:44.540
Yes.

04:45.040 --> 04:47.810
However, that wasn't all.

04:48.640 --> 04:50.270
With a new perspective,

04:50.270 --> 04:53.890
I obtained a method to 
change the colors of a flame.

04:55.310 --> 04:57.970
Tiny lights, floating in the darkness...

04:57.970 --> 05:02.550
they may look like the torches of 
war, or like the lights of fireflies.

05:02.550 --> 05:07.320
Each and every material and phenomenon 
holds more than one meaning.

05:07.650 --> 05:10.330
So does the black powder, and 
so do you, Professor Michel.

05:10.330 --> 05:15.330
There is nothing which exists solely 
to bring misfortune to others.

05:16.570 --> 05:20.630
And you plotted all of this 
to make me understand that?

05:21.460 --> 05:23.210
Why would you go so far?

05:23.670 --> 05:26.720
Because I am your student.

05:29.120 --> 05:31.650
If you wish to repudiate 
someone else's research,

05:31.650 --> 05:34.380
you must show results as counter-evidence.

05:35.120 --> 05:38.020
If you're an alchemist, that is.

05:38.580 --> 05:42.600
<i>Without substantiation, the professor 
would never change his thinking.</i>

05:43.400 --> 05:44.300
<i>That's why...</i>

05:45.820 --> 05:49.100
I will devote all of myself 
to trying to persuade you.

05:49.700 --> 05:51.950
Observe with your own eyes.

05:52.390 --> 05:54.370
Something which you have created...

05:54.370 --> 05:56.770
is exhibiting a value 
which you did not know of.

05:56.770 --> 05:58.070
Just look at it!

06:03.900 --> 06:08.780
I understand flame reactions and the 
effect of black powder, and yet...

06:09.720 --> 06:12.260
I never imagined a use like this existed.

06:44.430 --> 06:46.830
You're amazing, Rishe.

06:47.250 --> 06:49.900
No, you're the amazing one, Professor.

06:50.770 --> 06:55.230
I'm sure that there are other things 
which you thought could only be poisons

06:55.230 --> 06:57.720
which have other splendid uses.

06:58.330 --> 07:03.880
After all, you're the most 
brilliant alchemist in all the world!

07:10.720 --> 07:12.210
I see.

07:12.970 --> 07:19.240
So, I was able to create the source 
of something that beautiful.

07:26.720 --> 07:28.820
<i>It seems they all launched safely.</i>

07:35.490 --> 07:37.180
Thank you.

07:37.180 --> 07:39.580
It was really a lot of work.

07:40.780 --> 07:43.350
Could you give this to everyone for me?

07:43.910 --> 07:46.020
This? What is it?

07:46.480 --> 07:48.900
<i>The amount of black powder
 and where it was set...</i>

07:48.900 --> 07:52.250
<i>Because I saw his experiment 
planner in my third life,</i>

07:52.250 --> 07:55.260
<i>I could narrow down the possibilities, 
even in this large capital city.</i>

07:56.240 --> 07:58.580
<i>After that, I took the 
professor's area of activity,</i>

07:58.580 --> 08:01.800
<i>and looked for spots that 
matched the right conditions.</i>

08:02.740 --> 08:08.870
<i>The rest was all thanks to everyone involved 
in this matter doing their jobs perfectly.</i>

08:10.480 --> 08:13.900
Your Highness's retainers really 
are exceptional, aren't they?

08:18.330 --> 08:20.010
<i>Lord Lawvine?</i>

08:20.990 --> 08:22.620
As you ordered.

08:22.620 --> 08:23.590
Good work.

08:24.140 --> 08:25.440
Michel Hévin.

08:25.440 --> 08:28.320
This incident. You will 
have to explain yourself.

08:28.320 --> 08:30.160
Wait, Lawvine!

08:30.160 --> 08:32.570
I will take charge of that person.

08:32.570 --> 08:33.870
I cannot allow that.

08:33.870 --> 08:34.820
What?

08:34.820 --> 08:38.020
This individual declared that he 
would cause an incident here,

08:38.020 --> 08:40.730
on land governed by His Majesty, the emperor.

08:40.730 --> 08:43.940
Even though the order comes from 
you, Prince Theodore,

08:43.940 --> 08:46.460
I cannot hand him over to you.

08:54.250 --> 08:56.630
What is this commotion, Lawvine?

08:58.550 --> 09:00.040
Prince Arnold.

09:01.260 --> 09:04.640
I received a report of an individual 
making nefarious declarations.

09:04.640 --> 09:08.900
Believing him to be connected to the 
large flames seen in the air just now,

09:08.900 --> 09:11.800
I've captured him and 
intend to interrogate him.

09:12.240 --> 09:13.780
I see.

09:13.780 --> 09:15.540
Prince Arnold, earlier, those—

09:15.540 --> 09:16.390
Rishe.

09:16.910 --> 09:18.280
That is unnecessary.

09:21.590 --> 09:23.040
That phenomenon just now...

09:23.040 --> 09:27.170
it was no more than a scholar of Coyolles 
demonstrating a new technology.

09:30.210 --> 09:34.840
Why would a Coyolles scholar unveil a 
new technology here, in our country?

09:39.280 --> 09:43.470
Our empire will be forming a technological 
partnership with Coyolles.

09:59.490 --> 10:02.190
In exchange for providing military 
instruction to Coyolles,

10:02.190 --> 10:06.830
we will be borrowing their precision 
machining techniques and academic knowledge.

10:06.830 --> 10:08.800
Those flowers of flame we saw earlier...

10:08.800 --> 10:13.250
served as proof that Coyolles possesses 
technologies unknown to our empire.

10:14.130 --> 10:15.460
Do you understand?

10:18.700 --> 10:19.760
Go.

10:20.350 --> 10:21.180
Sir.

10:22.120 --> 10:23.470
Lord Lawvine.

10:24.140 --> 10:28.140
I apologize for hiding my 
identity all this time.

10:34.200 --> 10:35.280
Michel!

10:35.280 --> 10:39.450
I'm happy for your help forming this 
alliance, but that took me completely by surprise!

10:39.450 --> 10:40.340
Kyle.

10:40.950 --> 10:43.880
If you wanted to unveil the 
results of your research,

10:43.880 --> 10:47.200
there must have been methods which would 
have caused less trouble for others.

10:47.200 --> 10:48.310
You have it wrong.

10:48.870 --> 10:50.790
The truth is that lives would have—

10:50.790 --> 10:52.150
Professor Michel.

10:52.580 --> 10:55.710
Right now, please just stay quiet 
and let him be angry with you.

11:00.430 --> 11:02.470
I'm sorry, Kyle.

11:02.470 --> 11:04.280
I'm sorry, Rishe.

11:04.770 --> 11:05.580
Michel?

11:06.310 --> 11:07.720
I won't do it any more.

11:08.400 --> 11:11.520
My theory was hugely flawed.

11:11.520 --> 11:12.900
I understand that now.

11:15.620 --> 11:18.400
I promise you that I will never do it again.

11:21.150 --> 11:23.640
Then, I shall make the proper arrangements.

11:30.480 --> 11:33.920
I will say this: I am not acting 
out of kindness towards them.

11:34.320 --> 11:37.920
It's abundantly clear that he 
was plotting something unsavory.

11:38.180 --> 11:41.360
However, if he were publicly 
treated as a criminal,

11:41.360 --> 11:43.380
my father, the emperor, would hear of it.

11:43.380 --> 11:45.950
That's why I made use of your plan.

11:45.950 --> 11:48.460
Yes. Thank you.

11:48.940 --> 11:52.500
After I explain the details 
regarding the professor,

11:52.500 --> 11:54.380
I look forward to your 
judgment on the matter.

11:55.130 --> 11:56.690
How commendable of you.

11:56.690 --> 11:59.640
If I choose to kill and 
dispose of him in secret,

11:59.640 --> 12:02.200
I will hear no complaints from you.

12:06.620 --> 12:08.200
Prince Arnold.

12:10.050 --> 12:11.200
What is it?

12:12.130 --> 12:17.090
The truth is, the person who invented 
the pocket watch was Professor Michel.

12:20.860 --> 12:23.610
If we will be conducting joint 
research with Coyolles,

12:23.610 --> 12:27.350
won't Professor Michel's knowledge be needed?

12:29.350 --> 12:30.830
What will you do?

12:31.350 --> 12:32.720
You...

12:35.110 --> 12:37.310
No matter how I look at 
this, you were confident

12:37.310 --> 12:39.730
you could convince me 
from the very beginning.

12:39.730 --> 12:41.120
How could I be?

12:41.120 --> 12:44.080
The only thing I was confident of was that

12:44.080 --> 12:47.550
Your Highness would be 
interested in the professor.

12:49.740 --> 12:53.870
The people in town will 
have seen those fireworks.

12:53.870 --> 12:56.130
When people learn that 
they were from Coyolles,

12:56.130 --> 12:58.620
I think they will support the alliance, too.

12:59.430 --> 13:01.070
They probably will.

13:01.070 --> 13:01.930
Yes.

13:03.750 --> 13:06.440
So, those are called fireworks?

13:06.440 --> 13:09.050
Yes, that's what I've named them.

13:10.570 --> 13:15.160
I wanted you to see those 
fireworks, Your Highness.

13:17.250 --> 13:22.030
The black powder used in fireworks 
is a dangerous substance.

13:22.030 --> 13:24.790
However, depending upon how it's used,

13:24.790 --> 13:28.670
it can also create a beautiful sight the 
likes of which no one has seen before.

13:29.760 --> 13:35.090
If you learned that, then you would 
carve a path to many more possibilities.

13:35.600 --> 13:37.580
That's my thinking on it.

13:39.660 --> 13:46.780
<i>Right now, he may still believe that 
all of his abilities are meant for war,</i>

13:47.680 --> 13:50.490
<i>but one day, I'm certain...</i>

13:55.920 --> 14:00.650
This medicine will help with
 seasickness on your journey home.

14:00.650 --> 14:03.100
The flavor is as awful as ever, though.

14:03.100 --> 14:06.780
Compared to the suffering of 
seasickness, it's nothing.

14:08.230 --> 14:09.290
Lady Rishe.

14:10.320 --> 14:12.230
Truly, thank you so very much.

14:12.680 --> 14:15.200
It's only because you lent us your strength

14:15.200 --> 14:18.670
that Prince Arnold formed an 
alliance with our kingdom.

14:18.670 --> 14:24.170
No, it was Coyolles' sound technological 
prowess and support of academic research.

14:24.170 --> 14:27.920
This is all the result of you doing 
everything in your power, Prince Kyle.

14:33.580 --> 14:36.680
I think that your husband 
is far too magnanimous.

14:37.290 --> 14:38.940
Not at all, Professor.

14:38.940 --> 14:41.160
He's telling you that in this joint venture,

14:41.160 --> 14:44.690
you should continue producing 
the very best of results.

14:44.690 --> 14:48.760
It's a severe punishment which the average 
person wouldn't be able to shoulder.

14:48.760 --> 14:51.770
Yes, I suppose it is.

14:53.260 --> 14:56.380
"Create things which will make 
the world more wonderful."

14:56.380 --> 14:59.980
I've never done any research 
in that area before...

15:01.800 --> 15:02.970
but I'll do my best.

15:08.000 --> 15:09.900
I wanted to apologize to you.

15:11.270 --> 15:15.750
I was mistaken when I said that you 
weren't suited to being an empress.

15:16.220 --> 15:18.260
You're more than suited to it.

15:19.870 --> 15:23.070
But it's true that I see it as a shame.

15:24.660 --> 15:26.350
You won't regret it?

15:26.350 --> 15:29.610
A life as the bride of Arnold Hein.

15:30.000 --> 15:35.670
Right now, what I most want to know about 
is the man who will become my husband.

15:35.670 --> 15:39.000
I want to know him more than I want 
to know any research result or theory.

15:41.020 --> 15:43.380
And so we part for a time.

15:44.530 --> 15:47.960
Let's meet again, my student.

15:50.480 --> 15:51.340
Yes!

15:57.230 --> 16:00.100
Professor Michel was taken aback.

16:00.100 --> 16:02.560
He said Prince Arnold is "too magnanimous."

16:05.410 --> 16:08.380
Rather than making a fuss over 
something which ended in failure,

16:08.380 --> 16:11.860
making good use of him makes 
more sense. That's all.

16:12.400 --> 16:13.930
Thank you.

16:22.420 --> 16:25.500
I have one more thing to report.

16:30.760 --> 16:32.040
It's finished?

16:32.040 --> 16:32.950
Yes.

16:33.760 --> 16:36.700
I wanted to see the finished 
piece with you, Your Highness,

16:36.700 --> 16:38.460
so I haven't opened it yet.

16:38.960 --> 16:40.390
I'm sure it's lovely.

16:39.510 --> 16:40.390
Rishe.

16:42.060 --> 16:44.770
Showing me that you're wearing 
that ring is unnecessary.

16:50.070 --> 16:52.780
By unnecessary, you mean...

16:52.780 --> 16:54.320
I told you.

16:54.320 --> 16:59.560
The only thing that I requested of you 
was to allow me to gift you a ring.

17:02.480 --> 17:07.290
I have no right to wish 
for any more than that.

17:09.290 --> 17:11.690
You may have allowed me to gift you with it,

17:11.690 --> 17:14.800
but you needn't wear something 
which doesn't meet your standards.

17:15.280 --> 17:18.400
You should wear only that which you like,

17:18.400 --> 17:20.310
with no regard for the gazes of others.

17:20.310 --> 17:21.800
Choose freely.

17:27.520 --> 17:28.310
No.

17:29.000 --> 17:30.070
What?

17:30.500 --> 17:32.400
When they were measuring my size,

17:32.400 --> 17:35.400
I chose the third finger 
on my left hand, didn't I?

17:35.910 --> 17:36.960
Yes.

17:36.960 --> 17:42.980
In my country, when people are married, the 
husband places a ring on the wife's third finger.

17:46.000 --> 17:50.590
I long to experience that sort of ritual.

17:53.460 --> 17:56.070
I want to wear this ring 
for the marriage ceremony,

17:56.070 --> 17:58.220
and I will chose my dress to match it!

17:58.220 --> 18:00.320
You say that it's unnecessary,

18:00.320 --> 18:03.100
but I'm going to wear this ring everywhere!

18:03.100 --> 18:03.720
Rishe.

18:03.720 --> 18:08.230
If anything, I've been restraining 
myself from putting it on immediately!

18:09.220 --> 18:13.320
So, Prince Arnold, please 
put it on my finger for me.

18:13.320 --> 18:15.660
I'm not wearing gloves right now.

18:18.990 --> 18:22.030
It's all right, even without them.

18:26.200 --> 18:29.180
I just really want it to happen right now.

18:29.710 --> 18:30.660
So...

18:32.230 --> 18:34.070
Please, Your Highness.

19:12.390 --> 19:13.380
Rishe.

19:18.990 --> 19:20.340
May I touch you?

19:26.390 --> 19:27.270
Yes.

19:33.740 --> 19:35.960
Hey, don't hold your breath.

19:35.960 --> 19:37.730
I'm not holding my breath!

19:38.500 --> 19:41.400
I've simply forgotten how 
to breathe, that's all.

19:42.780 --> 19:43.980
<i>He laughed!</i>

20:04.560 --> 20:06.830
Have you remembered how to breathe?

20:06.830 --> 20:08.420
Yes, somehow.

20:18.280 --> 20:19.280
Rishe.

20:23.020 --> 20:24.060
It's done.

20:35.330 --> 20:39.440
It really is exactly the same 
color as Your Highness's eyes.

20:40.920 --> 20:45.010
Just wearing this ring makes me feel 
like I can accomplish anything.

20:48.760 --> 20:50.700
What do you think?

20:51.440 --> 20:52.170
Yes.

20:59.360 --> 21:02.570
It puts me in an even better 
mood than I'd imagined.

21:07.760 --> 21:08.930
Your Highness...

21:08.930 --> 21:09.780
What is it?

21:10.490 --> 21:13.990
The number of things I want 
to ask of you has increased.

21:13.990 --> 21:17.460
Tell me. Right now, I'd grant you anything.

21:19.890 --> 21:22.380
I want to go on a journey 
with you, Your Highness.

21:22.380 --> 21:23.390
A journey?

21:23.390 --> 21:28.340
Yes. A journey to see all of the 
beautiful things in this world.

21:28.340 --> 21:30.760
Not just fireflies and fireworks...

21:30.760 --> 21:37.440
I want to go and find many more things 
that you think are lovely and beautiful.

21:38.500 --> 21:41.480
Thanks to you, I've found 
one more of those things.

21:41.480 --> 21:42.080
What?

21:42.550 --> 21:44.110
What could it be?

21:45.530 --> 21:46.510
What indeed?

21:46.990 --> 21:50.690
If you don't know, then I won't tell you.

21:50.690 --> 21:52.160
Th-That isn't fair!

21:52.160 --> 21:55.080
Do you really think an average person 
can measure up to one of your riddles?

21:55.080 --> 21:57.730
An average person would not explode

21:57.730 --> 22:00.900
a mysterious compound in the sky 
over their betrothed's home.

22:09.570 --> 22:14.140
Though, I don't think this riddle 
is so very difficult to solve.

22:22.040 --> 22:24.770
<i>Right now, they may only be 
the slightest of changes...</i>

22:25.680 --> 22:30.470
<i>but as one piles on another, little by 
little the future should change, too.</i>

22:31.600 --> 22:36.500
<i>I hope to see a beautiful future 
together with Prince Arnold.</i>

22:38.970 --> 22:44.030
<i>In this life, that is the great 
objective I have found for myself.</i>
